menu "USB HID (subsys/usb_hid)"

    config USB_HID_REPORT_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Input report queue depth"
        default 8
        range 1 64
        help
            Reports buffered ahead of the interrupt IN endpoint. Raising it absorbs
            more producer jitter at the cost of latency and 66 bytes of RAM per slot.
            A full queue makes usb_hid_report_send() return ESP_ERR_NO_MEM.

    config USB_HID_EP_SIZE
        int "Default interrupt IN endpoint size (bytes)"
        default 64
        range 1 64
        help
            wMaxPacketSize when usb_hid_config_t.ep_size is 0. 64 is the full-speed
            interrupt maximum and also the largest report that can be sent.

    config USB_HID_POLL_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Default bInterval (ms)"
        default 1
        range 1 255
        help
            Host polling interval when usb_hid_config_t.poll_interval_ms is 0. On
            full-speed USB one frame is 1 ms, so 1 is the hardware floor (CON-02,
            SYS-HID-001). Larger values reduce bus load and host CPU at the cost of
            report latency.

endmenu
